#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557370} :activity/id #uuid "1f6d27b5-729c-512f-8bbb-fd371c843cf4" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050149 :topic/id #uuid "30edc058-70f2-5a72-9472-b7c90e677423" :topic/math-academy-id 1275} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557353 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "056ae85b-4497-51c3-bf0f-16db555df25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556442} {:answer/id #uuid "893a2d02-47a2-54d1-80f0-24b55f689ea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556754} {:answer/id #uuid "9e8e098e-a66d-5126-99c7-db91b01066aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "82" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556816} {:answer/id #uuid "a7188c0a-2793-54f6-a856-19adbe5707e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556841} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4e118b-ddd2-55e0-a765-c19e81224e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556923}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556923} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bd6e77c-1825-574d-9544-ad954df128e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c86bcf22-54c7-51dc-bd7b-9dc7538670ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-67785" :question/problem "![](images/27/27dc9ff8452d9a9aa95322492549ba0eabed5f68a7aa2e586ebe239143268bde.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/da/da7cc00005fbeb686443e2075009fda7c68f6d379a8ddb924a7dfe5b60e6ab16.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} \\\\  & =40\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈38.637,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 12\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{67.2}^{∘} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{67.2}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈27.656,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & =38.637+27.656 \\\\  & =66.293\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $66.$"} :step/id #uuid "3f0057db-8c02-55c7-898f-3136c6331c68" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557371}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557370 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00d6fe5b-b93a-5b3a-b3ae-957d16951d55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{22}{3}\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556429} {:answer/id #uuid "16b5e456-0628-5b28-9973-d24a67f59883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556479} {:answer/id #uuid "42dfb8fe-2ca7-5bf5-a862-8097a357954b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556578} {:answer/id #uuid "d645e81a-5337-5246-a811-91c0e07d93c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556952} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb5a129-5ab4-5d2c-9e01-2c562f075800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557057}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556578} :answer-field/id #uuid "04104815-55f0-5585-b546-93a2c497895f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e987c676-ae94-5f92-bdbb-ee11dc914f54" :question/math-academy-id "q-43310" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cce0e775722bbaaa8eeeb60a7cd097e8ad59b7c83c838f072416112aed657e33.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{21}{4}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=3\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{21}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{21}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 3\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{21}{4} & =\\frac{3b}{4} \\\\ 3b & =21 \\\\ b & =7\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=7\\text{cm}.$"} :step/id #uuid "7b22a461-459d-538c-a7ad-2b24ce04d8e3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557353}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557371 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557293 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65d7e23d-a662-543a-949a-9f1103f2f026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556669} {:answer/id #uuid "718ad878-e04a-5234-a710-bf3756d5dd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556688} {:answer/id #uuid "7822939c-8917-5fa9-999c-a9b7716110f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "14\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556703} {:answer/id #uuid "863c7b23-cd66-50d9-b292-999cccff557f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556747} {:answer/id #uuid "8fbfadd0-9675-506a-9f67-970459a5eb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556778}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556703} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1ee5adb-4e16-5916-9acc-b73f1caa075b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b105592d-99b2-5bf4-877e-0bc7baf37cd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161105" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0b460a07026e489fb7c63dad99c04c7e44540138632626dcd3ebcafb5c0a93d3.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $52{\\text{ in}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9\\cdot 16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{66}^{∘} \\\\  & =72\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{66}^{∘} \\\\  & =65.775… \\\\  & ≈66{\\text{ in}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of  $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =66-52 \\\\  & =14\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "80b2a081-7fde-5691-bde6-6ceee92db580"}] :activity/title "The Area of a General Triangle" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556410}]}
